The network shows road distances in kilometres. Its supplied minimum spanning tree contains $AB$, $BC$, $CD$ and $DE$.
Find the shortest path from $A$ to $E$ in the full network. Does it lie on the supplied tree? Compare its distance with the route along that tree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},x=13mm,y=13mm]
\coordinate (A) at (0,1); \coordinate (B) at (1,2.5); \coordinate (C) at (3,2.5); \coordinate (D) at (4,1); \coordinate (E) at (2,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$4$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,above] {$2$};
\draw (C)--(D) node[midway,above right] {$3$};
\draw (D)--(E) node[midway,below right] {$5$};
\draw (E)--(A) node[midway,below left] {$8$};
\foreach \v/\p in {A/left,B/above,C/above,D/right,E/below} {\fill (\v) circle (2pt); \node[\p] at (\v) {$\v$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
